homelab-dovecot (0.1.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * behind_haproxy now defaults to TRUE (was false), per direction:
    the safe/recommended posture (matches production, stays correct
    whether this host ends up alone or split) should be the path of
    least resistance, not something you have to know to turn on.
    Bumped its debconf prompt to high priority (was medium) so a plain
    interactive install actually sees and understands it, and the
    postinst's final summary now states plainly whether this host
    expects HAProxy in front and what happens if it isn't there yet

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 11:26:26 -0500

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 10:00:11 -0500

homelab-dovecot (0.1.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add an always-on SASL auth listener (inet_listener auth { port =
    12345 }, same bind-all/firewall-is-the-boundary reasoning as the
    existing LMTP listener) so homelab-postfix can authenticate
    submission SASL from a different host, not just when co-located.
    Confirmed this exact port against this project's own production
    dovecot
  * Add homelab-dovecot/behind_haproxy (debconf, default false,
    re-promptable on dpkg-reconfigure without a full reinstall) --
    when true, adds haproxy = yes to the imap-login listeners only
    (never LMTP/auth, which are direct Postfix-to-Dovecot calls that
    never pass through a proxy). Defaults off because enabling it for
    a Dovecot that isn't actually behind HAProxy would reject every
    direct IMAP/IMAPS connection outright

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Sun, 13 Sep 2026 09:59:51 -0500

